## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cryptographic isolation and operational controls for multi-tenant data in GCP. Assesses understanding of CMKs, envelope encryption, and how to integrate rotation, access policies, and automated validation into CI/CD to prevent data leakage and enable safe rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Customer-managed keys (CMKs) in Cloud KMS
- Envelope encryption for DB and object storage
- IAM Conditions and tenant-scoped service accounts
- Key rotation and versioning
- CI/CD validation and synthetic-tenant rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Encrypt with Cloud KMS (example)
const {KeyManagementServiceClient} = require("@google-cloud/kms");
const client = new KeyManagementServiceClient();
async function encrypt(plaintext, name) {
  const [result] = await client.encrypt({name, plaintext: Buffer.from(plaintext)});
  return result.ciphertext;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you audit and detect misconfigurations in KMS IAM Conditions and CMK bindings?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant CMKs vs centralized keys, and how would you mitigate overhead with automation?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in designing tenant-isolated logging architectures—a critical security requirement in multi-tenant SaaS platforms where log exposure can lead to data breaches.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Logging Router with tenant-specific sinks using label-based filtering
- IAM Conditions implementing least-privilege access controls
- Data Loss Prevention API for automatic PII redaction
- CI/CD pipeline integration with synthetic tenant provisioning
- Automated rollback mechanisms for isolation verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// Conceptual tenant sink configuration
const tenantSink = {
  name: `tenant-${tenantId}-sink`,
  filter: `resource.type="cloud_run_revision" AND labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  destination: `bigquery.googleapis.com/projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_logs`
};

// IAM Condition for tenant access
const tenantAccessCondition = {
  title: `Tenant ${tenantId} Log Access`,
  expression: `resource.name.startsWith("projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_")`
};
```

